WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.630
So, once you have a design system, and

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.510
you actually want to improve it further,

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.550
I'll show you a quick technique that is

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:08.470
actually going to change how you use

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.470
these design systems in order to just

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.910
continuously build out great components

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:14.950
that you can use for your other pieces

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.550
of software or for your builds. So, what

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.670
you see here is the System X design

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.550
system. And if you remember before, we

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:24.310
only had the guidance on the font. We

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.150
have guidance on the color palettes as

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.630
well as these line art animations. But

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:30.150
what I just asked Claude to do, which

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.070
I'll show you in a bit, is to think of a

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:34.670
few more components for us. So, if I

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.430
scroll down in here, apart from the data

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.110
tiers and apart from the color palettes,

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:40.390
now we have this component that now has

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.910
this split view dragging animation. If I

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:45.270
scroll down further, we have a grid

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.030
where we can actually have that

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.110
interactivity with our mouse pointer. It

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:51.590
also created for us five interactions

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.510
for typography. So, you can see here

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.750
when I hover over each of them, it gives

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.230
us that nicely designed animation for

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.390
the text, which is a lot more unique and

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.230
something that you wouldn't really find

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:04.229
from the default Claude code. And just

00:01:04.239 --> 00:01:05.470
to show you the session from which I

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:07.990
built those components, it's very simple

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.550
really. And this is actually something

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:11.510
that you can do once your usage is about

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:13.910
to run out. At least in terms of what's

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:15.110
available as of the time of this

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.190
recording, using Fable for something

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.310
like this is the most effective because

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:20.830
Fable's really good when it comes to

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:23.030
front end design. But let's say if I go

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.950
to the account and usage in here, and if

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:26.590
you see for instance that your weekly

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:29.390
limit is about to reset in a few hours

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.470
and you still have a lot of usage

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:33.190
remaining, what I would do if I were you

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.350
is I would run a prompt like this where

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.870
I will ask to improve our design system

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:40.070
with more interactive, visually striking

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:41.750
components. So, you can see I changed a

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:43.590
few skills in here. I gave it the

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.710
direction to improve the design system

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.510
X, the one that we just built. I also

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.750
used this skill called surprise me. And

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:51.350
that basically, what that does if you

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.190
install that is it will just force

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.150
Claude to completely vary its approach

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:57.830
in whatever it is that you are asking it

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.150
to do. I also invoke this align tree

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:02.350
skill in order for us just to be aligned

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:04.190
in terms of what it's about to do. So,

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.110
you can see here it gave me some

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:07.430
questions on how it's going to build out

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:09.630
those interactive components and where

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:11.390
it will put them. So, I just answered

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.030
those questions in turn and by the end

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:16.310
of it it gave us this HTML page that now

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.830
we have these nice animations that we

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:21.150
can use whenever we invoke this design

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:23.150
system. So, that is a great way for you

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.630
to further build out the components of

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:27.830
your design system so that you can just

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:31.320
improve it as time goes on.
